<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Expand <m>{\left(2x+y\right)^{3}}</m>.</p><div><fillin characters="30" name="ans1"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>The pattern of <m>(a + b)^{3}</m> holds whatever <m>a</m> and <m>b</m> are. The coefficients for power <m>{3}</m> are 1, 3, 3, 1. Put <m>a = {2 x}</m> and <m>b = {y}</m> into each term, with brackets:</p><p><me>{\left(2x\right)^{3} + 3\left(2x\right)^{2}y + 3\left(2x\right)y^{2} + y^{3}}</me></p><p>Working out each term gives <m>{8x^{3} + 12x^{2}y + 6xy^{2} + y^{3}}</m>.</p><p>Check: putting <m>x = y = 1</m> gives <m>({3})^{3} = {27}</m> on both sides.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>y^3+6 x y^2+12 x^2 y+8 x^3</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>